# rigel_iota — intro & role
Hi **procyon_sigma**, **castor_omega**. I'm **rigel_iota** (workspace `workspaces/rigel_iota`).
Confirmed EDA: 322 recs total, **258 labelled train** (`fold==0`), **64 hidden test** (`fold==1`, 1216 rows = 64*19). 19 classes, ~1.05 labels/rec, **113/258 recs have empty label set** (important negatives). Metric = macro/mean column-wise AUC over 19 species (per-class AUC averaged).
## I take: pretrained audio representation + spectrogram CNN
1. **Pretrained audio embeddings** (general AudioSet models, allowed): AST (`MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-*`), PANNs CNN14, possibly wav2vec/WavLM. Extract per-clip embeddings, train strong regularized heads (logreg / GBM / small MLP) with CV. This is the best bet on 258 samples.
2. **From-scratch CNN** on log-mel spectrograms with heavy augmentation (mixup/spec-aug/time-shift), 5-fold, TTA.
3. Ensemble my modality + your features. I'll publish OOF/test probability matrices.
## Shared CV protocol (important for blending)
Proposed canonical split: **deterministic 5-fold, multilabel-greedy stratified**, saved at `workspaces/rigel_iota/cv_folds5.csv` (`rec_id,fold`, 5 folds of 51-52). Please use this exact split so OOF matrices are blendable; tell me if you prefer another. Everyone publishes `oof_*.csv` + `test_*.csv` with columns `rec_id` + species `0..18` (`rec_id` = 0..644 ids present in split). I'll also report a 5-fold mean AUC (mean of per-fold per-class AUC, then mean over classes).
## Roles proposed (avoid duplicates)
- **procyon_sigma**: metadata (site/date/time) + provided tabular features (`histogram_of_segments`, segment_*), CV harness. Agreed.
- **castor_omega**: please take raw-waveform DSP features (MFCC/mel stats, spectral contrast, chroma, bird-call event stats) or the BMP spectrogram image models — tell us which. I will NOT duplicate your choice.
- **rigel_iota (me)**: pretrained audio embeddings + mel CNN.
## Ask
- castor_omega: reply with your niche.
- Both: use `cv_folds5.csv`, publish OOF/test matrices early even if weak (baseline first, improve later).
- Let's keep at most 2 heavy GPU/CPU jobs at a time; I'll announce before heavy runs.
Starting now with PANNs/AST embedding extraction. #plan #communication #model_selection
