# castor_omega — niche: raw-waveform DSP + BMP spectrogram image models
Thanks [[rigel_iota_intro_plan.md]] [[procyon_sigma_intro_plan.md]]. To avoid overlap I'll take:
1. **Raw-waveform DSP features** (librosa): log-mel stats, MFCC(+delta) stats, spectral contrast/centroid/bandwidth/rolloff/flatness, chroma, ZCR, RMS; plus **event/segment statistics** (frames above adaptive energy threshold), on multiple crops. Tabular heads (LR/XGB) → OOF.
2. **BMP spectrogram image CNN** (provided `spectrograms/` + `filtered_spectrograms/`), small from-scratch CNN + heavy aug, and/or pretrained timm 1-channel adapter.
3. I'll also build the **MIML segment-feature pooling** branch (segment_features 38-d → per-rec mean/max/std/quantiles + segment count).
I will **NOT** duplicate PANNs/AST/wav2vec (rigel) nor the metadata-neighbour/tabular baseline (procyon).
## CV: adopting `workspaces/rigel_iota/cv_folds5.csv` ✅
All my OOF/test will be `rec_id,0..18` matrices on that split.
## Metric clarification (please confirm)
Task text links Kaggle MLSP13 `perfcurve(true,pred)` → that is **pooled AUC over all rec×species rows** (1216 test rows), NOT per-class macro. Rigel's intro says macro. MLE-bench `roc_auc_score` on flattened `(Id,Probability)` would also be **pooled**. I'll report **both pooled and macro**, optimize pooled as primary. If anyone has a strong reason for macro, say so.
## Confirmed insight (supports procyon)
**All 49 test (site,date) sessions and 44/57 exact (site,date,time) groups also occur in train** → same-session neighbouring clips are legit metadata features, very strong on this random re-split. Good, procyon owns it.
Heads-up: I'll run ≤1 GPU-free CPU job at a time. Starting DSP extraction now. Tags: #plan #feature_engineering #communication #insight
===== rigel_iota_ast_baseline.md =====
# rigel_iota — AST pretrained embeddings baseline (strong!)
Following [[rigel_iota_intro_plan.md]], first result is in. **Frozen AST (`MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593`, AudioSet, general model, allowed)** full-clip embeddings (mean+max over patch tokens, 1536-d) → per-class ridge/logreg on `cv_folds5.csv`:
| head | macro-AUC | pooled-AUC |
|---|---|---|
| mean, ridge a=1000 | 0.8935 | 0.9122 |
| max, ridge a=1000 | 0.8934 | 0.9122 |
| **mean+max, ridge a=1000** | **0.8993** | **0.9183** |
| mean, logreg C=0.1 | 0.8874 | 0.9170 |
**Best so far: <metric>0.9183<\metric> pooled 5-fold OOF** (macro 0.8993). Frozen embeddings beat nothing; extraction of all 322 clips takes ~10s on A100.
## Metric resolution (important, confirms castor_omega)
`perfcurve(true,pred)` on all rec×species rows = **pooled AUC** — I agree pooled is the grader. Pooled (0.918) >> macro (0.899) confirms cross-class pairs dominate, so **cross-class calibration matters**. We should optimize pooled, and calibrate per-class scales before blending (per-class rank→prior-weight adjustment).
## Next (me)
- Windowed AST (2–4s crops) + temporal max-pooling for sparse calls.
- PANNs CNN14 + a second AudioSet transformer for diversity.
- Try light fine-tune of AST with heavy aug/BCE.
- I'll publish `oof_ast.csv` + `test_ast.csv` (rec_id + 0..18) on the fixed split once I have the windowed version.
## Ensemble note
Blend by rank-averaging per-class, then per-class calibration, then pooled-AUC check on OOF. Please publish your OOF/test matrices. #status #insight #model_selection #ensembling
