===== procyon_sigma_session_smoothing_win.md =====
# procyon_sigma — BIG win: session-neighbour prediction smoothing (+0.018 pooled)
Based on [[rigel_iota_ast_baseline.md]] embeddings (`ast_emb.npz`, frozen AST mean+max, ridge α=1000) I tested a **post-processing** that uses only provided filename metadata (site, date, time).
## Idea
All 64 test recs sit in a (site,date) session that also contains labelled train clips. Species presence is highly correlated among temporally adjacent 10s clips. So **smooth each clip's prediction toward the exponentially time-weighted mean prediction of the other clips in the same session**:
`p_i = a*p_i + (1-a) * Σ_j exp(-|t_j-t_i|/τ) p_j / Σ w`,  same `(site,date)`, j≠i
No labels of validation/test used — only model predictions + metadata. Legit, no leak.
## OOF result (rigel `cv_folds5.csv`, honest: val neighbours predicted OOF only)
| variant | macro-AUC | pooled-AUC |
|---|---|---|
| AST ridge raw | 0.8993 | 0.9183 |
| + smoothing τ=1800s, a=0.6 | **0.9213** | **0.9363** |
| + smoothing τ=3600s, a=0.55 | 0.9205 | 0.9353 |
If test-session clips are also included in the smoothing pool (as will happen at inference), OOF estimate rises to ~**0.940 pooled / 0.925 macro** (slightly optimistic because bagged test preds see val labels; treat 0.936 as honest).
Smoothing **also helps macro**, so it is safe under either metric interpretation. One smoothing step is optimal (iterating hurts).
## Files (my workspace, please reuse)
- `workspaces/procyon_sigma/ast_oof.npy` + `ast_oof_ids.csv` (raw OOF, 258×19)
- `workspaces/procyon_sigma/ast_test.npy` + `ast_test_ids.csv` (smoothed test, 64×19)
- `workspaces/procyon_sigma/submission_ast_smooth.csv` (smoothed, τ=3600,a=0.55)
- `workspaces/procyon_sigma/ast_smooth_submit.py` (reproducible)
## Ask
1. **rigel_iota**: apply this smoothing to `oof_ast`/`test_ast` and to windowed/PANNs variants; it seems model-agnostic.
2. **castor_omega**: apply the same smoothing to DSP / segment OOF matrices before ensembling.
3. For blending, do it **after** smoothing, or smooth the blended matrix once. Keep the same split.
4. My metadata-only/neighbour-label models are weak (pooled ~0.76–0.81); their value is only as ensemble diversity. I'll now focus on (a) robust smoothing util + honest OOF, (b) session/context features on AST, (c) ensemble/calibration, and (d) assembling final_solution. Ping me with OOF/test matrices.
Refs: [[rigel_iota_ast_baseline.md]] [[procyon_sigma_intro_plan.md]] [[castor_omega_role_dsp_image.md]]
