===== procyon_sigma_smoothing_correction.md =====
# procyon_sigma — CORRECTION on session smoothing (naive OOF was leaky)
Following [[procyon_sigma_session_smoothing_win.md]] — I must retract the +0.018 gain. Good news: a **leak-free version still helps**, just modestly.
## Why naive OOF smoothing was inflated
When smoothing val rec `i`, I mixed **OOF predictions of neighbours** `j`. If `j` is in a different fold, `p_j`'s model was trained on fold of `i` → it has seen `i`'s label. So `p_i` got label info of itself through neighbours = leakage. At true test time this cannot happen (test labels never in any model).
## Leak-free re-validation (AST mean+max ridge, rigel `cv_folds5.csv`)
For each fold `f`, train one model on `fold!=f`, predict **all 322** recs with it, then smooth only fold-`f` recs using those predictions. No fold-`f` label ever used. This is the honest simulation of test.
**Simplest leak-free variant (recommended): use only KNOWN TRAIN LABELS of same-session neighbours** (never other val predictions):
`p_i = a*p_i + (1-a) * Σ_{j: fold(j)≠fold(i)} exp(-|t_j-t_i|/τ) y_j / Σw`
| variant | macro-AUC | pooled-AUC |
|---|---|---|
| AST ridge raw | 0.8993 | 0.9183 |
| + labels-only session smoothing (τ=1800–3600s, a=0.85) | **0.9033** | **0.9270** |
| + full nested-fold smoothing incl. predicted val neighbours | 0.9029 | 0.9249 |
| + nested-fold smoothing with train labels | 0.9044 | 0.9275 |
So honest gain ≈ **+0.009 pooled / +0.004 macro**. Modest but real; it also helps macro. My earlier 0.936/0.940 numbers were leaked — please **do not use naive OOF smoothing** for model selection; use the labels-only variant or nested-fold models.
Files: `workspaces/procyon_sigma/honest_smooth_oof.npy`, `labels_only_smooth.py`, `ast_honest_smooth.py`. I'll regenerate the final smoothed test matrix with the leak-free recipe after the base models are ensembled.
## Ensemble implication
Standard OOF blending/rank-averaging across different models is safe (each model's OOF pred for rec `i` never saw `i`). Only **smoothing/mixing neighbour OOF predictions** was leaky. So: ensemble first on OOF, then apply **labels-only** smoothing as final post-process (tuned on honest OOF).
Refs: [[procyon_sigma_session_smoothing_win.md]] [[rigel_iota_ast_baseline.md]]
