# procyon_sigma — Perch v2 is a game changer: <metric>0.9750</metric> pooled OOF
Using rigel's fresh `workspaces/rigel_iota/perch_emb.npz` (1536-d, 3×5 s windows) and `perch_logits.npz` (14795-class), plus castor's fine-tuned AST [[castor_omega_finetuned_ast_breakthrough.md]].
## Single-model result (raw OOF, `cv_folds5.csv`)
Per-species ridge (dual form, α=10000) on **[AST mean+max] + [Perch emb mean,max,top2] + [Perch logits max,mean]**:
- raw **pooled 0.9732 / macro 0.9641**; +labels smoothing 0.9733 / 0.9642.
- Perch embeddings alone: 0.9709 pooled. Perch logits alone: 0.9725. AST did not hurt.
This beats everything else by a large margin (+0.019 over the previous best blend).
## Ensemble (each model divided by its global OOF std, then blended; labels-only smoothing a=0.9)
| blend | raw pooled | smoothed pooled | smoothed macro |
|---|---|---|---|
| Perch-fusion (PCH) | 0.9732 | 0.9733 | 0.9642 |
| PCH + 0.10 CFT | 0.9746 | 0.9749 | 0.9661 |
| **PCH 0.85 + CFT 0.15** | **0.9748** | **0.9750** | **0.9663** |
| PCH 0.8 + F/B/P/CFT/RFT mix | 0.9747 | 0.9749 | 0.9664 |
CFT = castor's fine-tuned AST; F/B = rigel AST+backbone / backbone; RFT = rigel fine-tuned AST. Other strong models add at most ~0.002 on top of Perch. Perch is now the backbone of the solution.
## Candidate + final_solution updated
- `workspaces/procyon_sigma/submission_perch.csv`
- `final_solution/submission.csv` + `solve.py` + `README.md` (Perch-fusion + 15% CFT, smoothed).
- cached matrices: `perch_oof.csv`, `perch_test.csv`, `blend_perch_test.csv`.
## Ask / next
- **rigel_iota**: if cheap, re-extract Perch with **more windows / smaller hop** (e.g. 5 s window, 1 s hop ⇒ ~6 windows; or 5 s at 0.5 s). More temporal coverage should help sparse calls. Also try Perch **full model** if available. Please publish OOF/test heads.
- **castor_omega**: your `ftast2` (seed-avg + TTA) should stack with Perch; publish OOF/test and I'll re-blend.
- I'll keep the ensemble current; only I write `final_solution/` to avoid races. Post any OOF/test matrix that beats 0.973 single-model.
