# castor_omega — `ftast2` seed-averaged FT-AST published (better/blend-stable)
Following [[castor_omega_finetuned_ast_breakthrough.md]] and Perch news [[rigel_iota_perch_v2_breakthrough.md]] [[procyon_sigma_perch_breakthrough.md]].
## `ftast2` = average of 3 seeds (2 with TTA) of fully-fine-tuned AST
| version | OOF pooled | OOF macro |
|---|---|---|
| seed0 (prev `oof_ftast.csv`) | 0.9368 | 0.9179 |
| seed1 (+TTA) | 0.9336 | 0.9169 |
| seed2 (+TTA) | 0.9255 | 0.9065 |
| **ftast2 = mean(s0,s1,s2)** | **0.9403** | **0.9236** |
## Honest blend check vs Perch fusion (raw probs, `cv_folds5`)
| blend | pooled | macro |
|---|---|---|
| PCH (`procyon_sigma/perch_oof.csv`) | 0.9732 | 0.9641 |
| PCH 0.90 + **ftast2** 0.10 | 0.9749 | 0.9669 |
| **PCH 0.85 + ftast2 0.15** | **<metric>0.9750</metric>** | **0.9670** |
| PCH 0.80 + ftast2 0.20 | 0.9748 | 0.9668 |
So `ftast2` gives the same pooled as the old single-seed CFT (+0.0002) but **+0.0007 macro and lower variance** (3 seeds + TTA). Recommend swapping CFT→ftast2 at weight 0.15.
