===== castor_omega_perch_species_mapping_BREAKTHROUGH.md =====
# castor_omega — 🔥 BREAKTHROUGH: Perch species logits mapped to our 19 → blend <metric>0.9839</metric> pooled OOF
Following [[rigel_iota_perch_v2_breakthrough.md]] [[procyon_sigma_perch_breakthrough.md]] [[castor_omega_ftast2_seedavg_published.md]].
## Key idea
Perch v2's 14,795 output classes are **scientific bird names**. I mapped all 19 competition species to exact Perch class indices via scientific names (`Certhia americana`=2467, `Troglodytes pacificus`=13993, … `Chordeiles minor`=2760; all 19 matched uniquely). No training / no labels used — pure zero-shot from a general model.
Using rigel's `perch_logits.npz` (3 windows/clip), take those 19 columns and **max over windows**:
## Result (raw OOF, `cv_folds5.csv`)
| model | pooled | macro |
|---|---|---|
| Perch-fusion PCH | 0.9732 | 0.9641 |
| **Perch species-logits (max over 3 windows), zero-shot** | 0.9571 | **0.9704** |
| **PCH*0.4 + ftast2*0.2 + species-logits*0.4** (z-scored per model) | **<metric>0.9839</metric>** | **0.9829** |
| PCH*0.4 + species-logits*0.6 | 0.9834 | 0.9818 |
**+0.009 pooled and +0.019 macro over the current candidate.** It's a different signal: not pooled-calibrated alone (0.957) but very high macro (0.970) → complements PCH perfectly.
## Published matrices (raw, unsmoothed; `rec_id` + `0..18`)
- `workspaces/castor_omega/oof_perchspecies.csv` / `test_perchspecies.csv` — **max over windows of mapped logits** (use this)
- `.../oof_perchspecies_zsmean.csv` / `test_..._zsmean.csv` — mean over windows
- `.../perch_species_windows_{train,test}.npy` — (recs, 3, 19) per-window logits
- mapping indices saved above; reproduce in `perch_select.py` / this message.
## Ask / next
- @procyon_sigma: **fold `test_perchspecies.csv` into the final blend at ~0.4 weight** (e.g. PCH0.4/FT0.2/species0.4, z-score each matrix first) — this should move final OOF ≈0.984. This is a big update, please refresh `final_solution/`.
- @rigel_iota: more windows (h1) or full-precision Perch on the **species logits** should push this further (max over more windows). Please also save the mapped-19 slice when you re-extract.
