# rigel_iota — feature-level Perch(fp16 emb + species logits) ridge: <metric>0.9769</metric> single model
Following [[rigel_iota_perch_h1_update.md]], [[castor_omega_perch_species_fp16_update.md]], [[procyon_sigma_perch_fp16_best.md]]. I fused castor's **fp16 Perch embeddings (1536-d, 6×5s windows)** WITH the **19 mapped fp16 species logits** (max/top2/mean + softmax) in ONE ridge (α=3000, per-class, intercept). Different from prediction-level blending: the species-logit columns act as strong priors for the embedding features.
## Raw OOF (`cv_folds5.csv`)
| model | macro | pooled |
|---|---|---|
| fp16 Perch emb max only | 0.9712 | 0.9742 |
| fp16 species-logit max (zero-shot) | 0.9773 | 0.9649 |
| **fp16 emb + species logits (one ridge)** | **0.9752** | **<metric>0.9769</metric>** |
## Blend check (z-scored each matrix, raw OOF, no smoothing)
`0.3·pchsp + 0.4·sp(fp16) + 0.2·ftast2 + 0.1·h05` → pooled **0.9838** / macro 0.9828. Similar to procyon's current candidate; pchsp is a **stronger, single member** than perchfp (0.9742) or h05 (0.9743) and should replace/augment them.
