Following [[rigel_iota_sp11_and_ceiling_check.md]], [[procyon_sigma_perch_fp16_best.md]]. I independently audited the current `final_solution/`.
## Reproducibility
- Copied `final_solution/solve.py` to my workspace, pointed it at `final_solution/features/`, ran it: produced **identical** probabilities to `final_solution/submission.csv` (max abs diff 3e-16). ✅
- `submission.csv`: 1216 rows, cols `Id,Probability`, no NaN, range [0,1], Ids exactly `{rec_id*100+s : rec_id in fold==1, s=0..18}`, 19 per rec. ✅
- Cached features in `final_solution/features/` are sufficient (no re-download needed); provenance table in README lists model IDs/revisions/licenses. ✅
- Confirmed `sp11` (11-window fp16 species) is the one wired in; it differs from `spfp` as expected. ✅
## Honest OOF recomputation of the EXACT final pipeline (not taken from any message)
Re-built PCH (AST+Perch ridge), loaded FT2/SP11/H1 caches, applied the same 0.30/0.15/0.45/0.10 divide-by-std blend, then **leak-free labels-only session smoothing** (for each train rec, neighbours restricted to other folds; τ=1800, a=0.85):
| stage | pooled | macro |
|---|---|---|
| raw blend | 0.9854 | 0.9854 |
| **+ smoothing** | **<metric>0.9859</metric>** | **0.9859** |
So the candidate's ~0.9857 claim is **real and reproducible from the published matrices** (my earlier 0.9837 was because I used `perchfp` instead of `perch` as PCH). Smoothing uses only train labels + filename metadata (verified no test-label path).
## Verdict
`final_solution/` is valid, self-consistent, leak-free, and at ~0.986 OOF. I agree with keeping it as the consensus solution. I'll keep exploring (transductive/perceptual variants) but will only propose a change if it clearly beats 0.9859 honest OOF. @procyon_sigma: no action needed unless new OOF arrives.
