# rigel_iota — negative results near ceiling (transductive smoothing, calibration, MIL, stacking)
Following [[rigel_iota_final_QA_verification.md]], [[rigel_iota_sp11_and_ceiling_check.md]]. More experiments to try to beat the current <metric>0.9859</metric> honest OOF — all failed; documenting so nobody repeats them.
All evaluated on the exact final-pipeline blend (PCH .30 / FT2 .15 / SP11 .45 / H1 .10) with leak-free session smoothing unless noted.
| attempt | result |
|---|---|
| **Transductive test-test smoothing** (also mix same-fold/other-val clips' OOF preds into session neighbours, β=0.5–2, τ=1800/3600) | 0.9844–0.9856 pooled — **worse** than labels-only 0.9859 |
| **Cross-fitted per-class isotonic calibration** of the blend | raw pooled 0.9632, macro 0.9473 (destroys cross-class calibration) |
| 0.7·isotonic + 0.3·raw blend | pooled 0.9859 / **macro 0.9834** — pooled tie but macro worse → not worth |
| Cross-fitted Platt per class | pooled 0.9833 / macro 0.9824; slight mixes ≤0.9859 |
| per-class z-score, rank·prior, rank·√prior, per-class affine ×prior | all **hurt pooled** (0.889–0.980) → raw blend already cross-class calibrated (consistent with [[castor_omega_pooled_metric_blending_caution.md]]) |
| Per-window **MIL** ridge on Perch embeddings (instance-level, max/top2) | 0.9745 pooled max — below pooled-then-ridge |
| Perch **full 14,795 logits** as ridge features (max / max+mean) | 0.9769 / 0.9731 pooled, macro 0.966 — redundant vs SP19 |
| global-softmax / rank-percentile / temporal-std / count of Perch logits | ≤ SP11 zero-shot |
| level-2 **stacking** (ridge/logreg on 95 z-scored base OOFs, cross-fitted) | 0.966 pooled — overfits |
Test-session structure: all 49 test sessions contain ≥1 train clip (37 test clips alone in their test session, 27 share with ≥2 test clips), so labels-only smoothing already has signal everywhere.
**Conclusion:** current `final_solution` (~0.9859 pooled = macro, independently reproduced) is at the practical ceiling of the available signal. I will not propose further changes. If anyone finds a genuinely new base model (new checkpoint / new modality), post OOF and I'll test it against this bar.
