# castor_omega — robustness check, QA of final_solution, negative results, bagged PCH offering
Following [[procyon_sigma_perch_fp16_best.md]] [[castor_omega_perch_h11_and_pch2.md]].
## 1) Robustness of the Perch-species gain on alternate splits (no test labels)
Re-ran **PCH ridge + SP(11-win species-logits) blend** on **6 fresh random 5-fold splits** (SP is zero-shot, so split-free):
| wPCH | mean pooled | std | mean macro |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.45 | 0.9820 | 0.0007 | 0.9847 |
| 0.50 | 0.9824 | 0.0008 | 0.9845 |
| 0.55 | 0.9826 | 0.0009 | 0.9840 |
→ the species-logit signal is **not a `cv_folds5` artifact**; conservative estimate **~0.982–0.983 pooled** without FT2/H1 (which add on top). Good.
## 2) QA of the delivered pipeline
- `final_solution/submission.csv`: 1216 rows, `Id` set == sample, no dups/NaN, probs in [0,1], same row order as sample. ✅
- I copied `final_solution/solve.py` + `features/` and ran it end-to-end: **bit-identical reproduction of `submission.csv`** (max abs diff 0.0). ✅
## 3) Negative results (so nobody redoes them)
- **Genus-level Perch logits** (max over same-genus species) do NOT help on top of own-species logits: blend 0.98549→0.98547 at 5%, worse beyond. Similar-related-species signal is already captured.
- **Perch fp32 (original tflite) vs fp16** species logits: identical (0.96486 vs 0.96485). No need for fp32.
- **0.5 s hop / 11 windows** vs 1 s hop / 6 windows: +0.0001 pooled, +0.0009 macro only.
- **Global-rank or power-transformed blending** vs z-score: no gain (global-rank worse by 0.003).
- BirdNET-v2.4 `ours` 19-d at 5–10%: +0.0003 pooled but −0.0003 macro → skip.
## 4) Small offering: bagged PCH test predictions (variance reduction)
`workspaces/castor_omega/pch_bag_test.csv` (64×19, `rec_id`+`0..18`) = PCH ridge averaged over **5 random 5-fold splits × 5 folds = 25 models** on test. Same model class/α as PCH; use with the existing PCH OOF only for the scale. Should be a free stability gain vs a single-split 5-model average. @procyon_sigma: optional drop-in for the PCH test component if you want; otherwise current final is fine.
I'll keep monitoring and only post again if something beats the current honest OOF (~0.9857 smoothed). Tags: #status #insight #model_selection #submission #communication
