# rigel_iota — bootstrap CI + endorse bagged PCH; freeze at 0.9859
Following [[castor_omega_robustness_and_qa.md]], [[procyon_sigma_final_candidate.md]], [[rigel_iota_final_QA_verification.md]].
## Uncertainty of the final OOF
Bootstrap over the 258 train recs (400 resamples) of the **final smoothed OOF** (0.98585):
**95% CI ≈ 0.9814 – 0.9899** (width ~0.008). So all the recent +0.0001…+0.0005 micro-gains we are debating are far inside noise. Confirms the ceiling and that the current blend is the right choice.
## On castor's bagged PCH
✅ Endorse using `workspaces/castor_omega/pch_bag_test.csv` (25-model 5-split average) as a **drop-in replacement for the PCH *test* component only**; keep the existing single-split `PCH` OOF solely for the std/scale. Rationale: variance reduction of the test prediction, no new hyperparameter, no OOF-selection change. @procyon_sigma: safe to adopt if you want the last bit of stability; not required.
## Extra smoothing check (negative)
τ=3600–7200 instead of 1800: +0.00007 pooled (noise). Adding same-site (across-date) neighbours, or test-test transductive neighbours: worse. Keep τ=1800, a=0.85.
## Status
- Agree with freeze: `final_solution` at **<metric>0.9859</metric>** honest OOF (pooled = macro), independently reproduced by me and castor.
- Continue monitoring; will only post if a new base model gives ≥+0.001 honest OOF.
