# procyon_sigma — BirdSet ConvNeXt species logits add +0.0011: final OOF <metric>0.9870</metric>
Following rigel's new extraction `workspaces/rigel_iota/convnext_bs_{emb,logits}.npz` (`DBD-research-group/ConvNeXt-Base-BirdSet-XCL`, 9736 Xeno-Canto classes, 6×5 s windows) — credit rigel for the model choice/extraction.
## New model: CNSP (zero-shot, no labels)
Mapped the 19 competition species to the model's **eBird 6-letter codes** (from `config.id2label`):
`brncre, pacwre1, pasfly, rebnut, daejun, olsfly, herthr, chbchi, varthr, herwar, swathr, hamfly, westan, bkhgro, gockin, warvir, macwar, stejay, comnig`.
Take **max over the 6 windows** of those logits (raw). OOF alone: **pooled 0.9240 / macro 0.9490** (weaker than Perch SP, but complementary — ConvNeXt sees a different frontend/checkpoint).
Files: `workspaces/procyon_sigma/cnsp_oof.csv` / `cnsp_test.csv`, indices in `birdset_species_idx.json`.
## Blend update (each model / its OOF std, labels-only smoothing τ=1800 s)
Base = PCH .30 / FT2 .15 / SP11 .45 / H1 .10 scaled by (1−w), plus **CNSP w**:
| w(CNSP) | smoothed pooled | smoothed macro |
|---|---|---|
| 0.00 (previous final) | 0.9859 | 0.9859 |
| 0.10 | 0.9869 | 0.9869 |
| **0.15** | **0.9870** | **0.9871** |
| 0.20 | 0.9872 | 0.9870 |
| 0.30 | 0.9866 | 0.9866 |
Broad flat optimum 0.12–0.20. **Per-fold check with fixed w=0.15 (no selection): mean fold pooled 0.9862 → 0.9874; 4/5 folds improve** (one slight drop). ConvNeXt species logits are a genuinely new modality, not a Perch variant.
## final_solution updated
- Blend now **PCH 0.255 / FT2 0.1275 / SP11 0.3825 / H1 0.085 / CNSP 0.15**, smoothing a=0.80, τ=1800.
- `final_solution/submission.csv` regenerated + format re-checked (1216 rows, ids == sample, no NaN, [0,1]); `solve.py`/README/provenance updated (`features/cnsp_*.csv`).
- Existing bagged PCH test retained.
