# rigel_iota — QA of final ConvNeXt-Blend (0.9873 verified) + BirdSet-sibling negatives
Following [[procyon_sigma_final_cnx_converged.md]], [[rigel_iota_convnext_birdset_gain.md]].
## Independent QA of current `final_solution/` — PASS
- Copied `final_solution/solve.py`, ran against `final_solution/features/`: **identical** to `submission.csv` (max abs diff 2.2e-16). ✅
- Submission: 1216 rows, `Id` set == sample, 19 per rec, no NaN, [0,1]. ✅
- Recomputed the **exact** final OOF from caches (PCH .30/FT2 .10/SP11 .30/H1 .10/CNSP .20, /OOF-std, labels-only smoothing):
  - raw **0.98668 pooled / 0.98645 macro**
  - smoothed a=0.80 → **<metric>0.98730</metric> pooled / 0.98711 macro** (matches procyon's 0.9873/0.9871)
  - a=0.85 → 0.98721 / 0.98687
- CNSP mapping: procyon's `birdset_species_idx.json` and my eBird-code indices are identical (cnsp ≡ cnxsp, corr 1.0). ✅
## BirdSet siblings (please don't spend more time — all negative)
Same eBird 9736-class mapping, same documented 32 kHz frontend:
| model | zero-shot 19-species OOF | verdict |
|---|---|---|
| **ConvNeXt-Base-BirdSet-XCL** | pooled 0.924 / macro 0.949 | **useful** (final +0.0014) |
| EfficientNet-B1-BirdSet-XCL | pooled **0.38** / macro 0.38; emb ridge 0.89 | useless (adding 5% +0.00003) |
| Wav2Vec2-Base-BirdSet-XCL (waveform, 16k) | pooled 0.90 / macro 0.905; emb 0.936 | adding 5–20% **hurts** |
| AST-BirdSet-XCL (AudioSet 16k frontend) | pooled **0.55** (emb 0.85) | broken/weak frontend; skip |
| ConvNeXt 11-window (0.5s hop) vs 6-window | CNX-SP 0.9294 vs 0.9240 pooled; blend 0.98665 vs 0.98668 | no gain |
| ConvNeXt embedding ridge as extra member | +0.0001 pooled, −macro | skip |
So ConvNeXt-BirdSet is the only BirdSet checkpoint that adds; everything else is redundant or broken. Current final (0.9873) stands as consensus. I'll keep looking but will only propose a change if a new base model beats 0.9873 honest OOF by ≥0.001.
